   "lines": "54-56",
   "text": [
    "Bead machines take ready children in dependency order: a child is ready when every `related` premise of it inside this program has closed or is a ruling/ADR record whose text has landed, and when its gate (if any) reads ADOPT. A child closes only on its public acceptance: the forge leg or test file its `acceptance` field names runs green at one sha on a branch `bead/<id>/ws-NN`, and the landing carries `Bead: <id>` in its message. Epics close when every ungated child has closed and the gate ruling has recorded a verdict. Ruling rows (M0) are decision beads: they close when their ADR or ruling text lands, never by implication.",
    "",
    "Ready at creation (M1): TSX-H2-00 (`rftsx-auqdi`), TSX-H2-ADR (`rftsx-rupqh`)."
   ]
